<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mojavensis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg most-unstable wavelength for D. mojavensis epicuticle at 2.4 µm (0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes R1 and R2. No-flux and periodic patches select the same radial-FFT bin (2.41388 µm) while the saturated std moves from 1.01072 (periodic) to 0.99918 (Neumann). Saturated FFT wavelengths track the square law: D. miranda 3.2825 µm vs analytic 3.2364 µm, focal small-grid 2.4139 µm, D. novamexicana 1.9754 µm vs analytic 1.9477 µm, in that order. Dispersion Pearson r remains 0.99323 (RMSE 0.02405). GIF unchanged: 14 frames, 640×480, CV 87.1. Image fitness 85.7 = 0.55*87.1 + 0.30*82 + 0.15*88. Age 0 Ma. Scale 2.4 µm (2.38e-06 m). Overall 87.0/100 (faithfulness 86.7, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0e0828eed603126b2ece796473b70906c8bb4076; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_mojavensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mojavensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0e0828eed603126b2ece796473b70906c8bb4076, image/png, 491888 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 33eeba72316e26acf05bde40511d05c5fba8645851653c61c93b7241b21bfa3f (sha256 33eeba72316e26acf05bde40511d05c5fba8645851653c61c93b7241b21bfa3f), spec_fingerprint b1989635e560992257bdc385b54a49911ad758777fefbeab3e3411ca482c2805. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b1989635e560992257bdc385b54a49911ad758777fefbeab3e3411ca482c2805; artifact_sha256: 33eeba72316e26acf05bde40511d05c5fba8645851653c61c93b7241b21bfa3f; input_dataset_sha256: {drosophila_mojavensis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=7ab7a539471b2219..., drosophila_mojavensis_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=f68e7b21de8d6b97..., drosophila_mojavensis_wikimedia_female.png=7615839cbc796270..., metrics.json=154f7148e93186ae...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-mojavensis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and linear dispersion | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Matzkin et al. 2006 and 2012, Allan & Matzkin 2019: cactus-host differentiation in D. mojavensis | Drosophila 12 Genomes Consortium 2007 placed D. mojavensis in the repleta group; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv calibrated so the most-unstable wavelength equals 2.38e-06 m | Chronospecies wavelengths via λ ∝ √D at fixed Jacobian and R=80, now checked by saturated FFTs | No-flux Laplacian as a boundary control; it does not move the radial-FFT bin on this grid | Activator composited onto the canonical gallery plate for the GIF; transfer_boundary: Campaign chronoseries order (miranda before mojavensis before novamexicana) is not a cladogram | The 2.4 µm length is the catalog detail tier, not a length reported in the Matzkin papers; does_not_claim: That 2.38 µm was read off a D. mojavensis micrograph in the cited papers | That the gallery plate's 100 µm scale bar is this slot's phenomenon scale | That a second assessor scored this audit | That nanopubs were signed (no ~/.nanopub/profile.yml)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

